,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.94071825,"data":"╭─────────────────────────────── Latest Detail ────────────────────────────────╮\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940742326,"data":"│   ✅ Agent Finished                                                          │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940746128,"data":"│     ... (1 earlier lines)                                                    │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940758046,"data":"│     The bug was caused by an overly restrictive assertion in                 │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940760204,"data":"│ `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` within the `analyze_param` function.         │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940762098,"data":"│ Specifically, it asserted that `depends` must be `None` when the type        │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940763976,"data":"│ annotation was `Response`, `Request`, or `WebSocket`, which prevented these  │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940765782,"data":"│ types from being used with `Depends` for dependency injection.               │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940767668,"data":"│                                                                              │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940769481,"data":"│     I modified the conditional check to ensure that this special handling    │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.94077148,"data":"│ (and the associated assertions) only occurs if `depends` is indeed `None`.   │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940773297,"data":"│ This allows users to use `Depends` to provide or modify the response object, │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940775184,"data":"│ while still maintaining the original behavior for cases where no dependency  │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940776982,"data":"│ is specified.                                                                │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940778863,"data":"│                                                                              │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940780685,"data":"│     The fix was verified by creating a reproduction test case that used both │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940782638,"data":"│ `Annotated[Response, Depends(...)]` and `response: Response = Depends(...)`  │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.94078453,"data":"│ syntax, both of which now work correctly and allow modifying response        │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.94078633,"data":"│ headers.                                                                     │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940788137,"data":"│                                                                              │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940789938,"data":"│     ```python                                                                │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940791753,"data":"│     # Example of the now-supported usage:                                    │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940794189,"data":"│     @app.get(\"/endpoint\")                                                    │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940796253,"data":"│     def endpoint(response: Annotated[Response, Depends(modify_response)]):   │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940798173,"data":"│         return {\"message\": \"Hello World\"}                                    │\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":667.940800222,"data":"│     ```                                                                      │\n"}
